<item>
      <title>Collision of two trains in Egypt kills at least seven</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/08/egypt-two-trains-deadly-collision</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;President orders prompt investigation after one train derails in collision in al-Ayyat about 50km from Cairo&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Seven people were killed and at least 125 injured when two trains collided on Sunday south of the Egyptian capital, Cairo, officials said.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The crash occurred in al-Ayyat district in Giza province, about 50km (30 miles) south of Cairo, when a train travelling to Fayoum province crashed into the rear of a train heading to the southern province of Aswan, according to the transport ministry.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/08/egypt-two-trains-deadly-collision"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
